## What you can do

- Monitor your accounts and credit reports for any unexpected
  activity.
- If you live in the United States, you may obtain a free credit
  report from each of the three nationwide consumer reporting
  agencies once every 12 months at AnnualCreditReport.com or by
  calling 1-877-322-8228.
  - Equifax: 1-800-685-1111 — www.equifax.com
  - Experian: 1-888-397-3742 — www.experian.com
  - TransUnion: 1-800-916-8800 — www.transunion.com
- You may also report identity theft to the U.S. Federal Trade
  Commission at IdentityTheft.gov or 1-877-438-4338.
- If you live in the European Union or United Kingdom, you have the
  right to lodge a complaint with your national data protection
  authority. The full list is available at edpb.europa.eu/about-edpb/
  about-edpb/members_en.

## Your rights

